From 776f41cddc3a99d417bf7b9fa43c05451ecc0898 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:00:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] fix(trace): say which kept adjustments a style uses,
 and keep the boundary mode (ADR-396)

Adjustments are kept in one set across trace styles, but each style uses
only the controls it shows. "Settings edited" now appears only when the
used adjustments change what the selected style traces, so re-selecting
the default Detection, or keeping a manual band while automatic
detection runs, no longer marks the style as edited. The hint under the
preset says adjustments carry over to styles with the same control and
names the kept ones the style ignores, for example "Not used by Line
Art: Sensitivity." Reset trace settings still clears all of them.

Selecting Photo shading traces a boxed region with Crop, as before, but
no longer overwrites the operator's choice: switching back to another
style restores Enhance region if it was chosen.

